HostFuzz
========

HostFuzz is the artifact for the paper "HostFuzz: A Framework for Scalable BLE
Host Fuzzing via HCI Interaction" (NDSS 2027).

The original HostFuzz code in `crates/` and `apps/` is released under the
MIT OR Apache-2.0 license (see LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE).

This repository vendors third-party components:

- `deps/libafl` — LibAFL, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
  Upstream: https://github.com/AFLplusplus/LibAFL
- `deps/qemu-libafl-bridge` — QEMU with the LibAFL bridge, GPL-2.0.
  Upstream: https://github.com/AFLplusplus/qemu-libafl-bridge
  The GPL-2.0 license text is in `deps/qemu-libafl-bridge/COPYING`
  (and `COPYING.LIB` for the library parts). Because the fuzzer binaries
  statically link this QEMU-derived code, redistributed binaries built from
  this tree are subject to GPL-2.0. The complete corresponding source is
  included in this repository.
- Fuzzware (installed by `Dockerfile --target full`) — BSD-3-Clause.
  Upstream: https://github.com/fuzzware-fuzzer/fuzzware
- Demo firmware/application binaries are built from open-source BLE stacks:
  BlueKitchen BTstack (Apache-2.0), Zephyr (Apache-2.0), Apache NimBLE
  (Apache-2.0), and ESP-IDF BlueDroid (Apache-2.0). Their source code is not
  vendored here; the binaries are included only as fuzzing targets.

Security-testing inputs and detailed vulnerability reports for findings that
were still under coordinated disclosure at submission time are intentionally
not part of this artifact.
